    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green. Here's a summary of what I changed to unify `customerCode` + `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId`.\n\n## What was done\n\n**Format:** `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` with no internal separators, so the fixed-width trailing segments (FY=2, HASH8=8, CHK=1) are recoverable from the right regardless of region length. Verified in the audit output: `NSW2716E6609E1` (region `NSW`, FY `27` for a 2026-09 date, hash `16E6609E`, Luhn check `1`).\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n- **`util/MemberId.java`** (new, replaces deleted `util/CustomerCode.java`): `format(region, fy, hash8)` builds the core and appends `LuhnCheckDigit.compute` over `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`; `region(...)` and `fiscalYear(...)` extract segments from the right, tolerating a `-<n>` collision suffix.\n- **`model/Owner.java`**: dropped `customerCode`, `membershipNumber` (and their columns/accessors); added `memberId` (`member_id` column).\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**: removed the `checkDigit` mapping; `memberId` maps automatically; `locality` now reads the region from the member id; `fiscalYear` now reads the FY segment from the member id (falling back to registration date when no id present).\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**: `assignDerivedFields` now sets `memberId` (removed the membership-number step); new `memberId(owner)` builder + `existingMemberIds()` for collision handling; `primaryIdentifier` returns the member id; audit line and structured `OWNER_CREATED` event now carry `memberId` (membership-number field dropped).\n- **`util/LuhnCheckDigit.java`, `util/Sha256Hex.java`**: doc references updated to the member id.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`**: replaced `customerCode` + `checkDigit` schemas with `memberId`; removed `membershipNumber`; updated `fiscalYear`/`locality` descriptions.\n- **DB schemas** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres): `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id` (widened), `membership_number` removed.\n\n**Test result:** `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS` (the `coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId` acceptance test, plus a clean compile of the OpenAPI-generated DTOs).",
